<div class="message message-tool active">  <div class="message-header">    <div class="role-badge"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="chevron lucide lucide-chevron-right"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg> <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-terminal"><polyline points="4 17 10 11 4 5"/><line x1="12" x2="20" y1="19" y2="19"/></svg> tool</div>    <div class="timestamp">2026-09-05 00:31:28</div>  </div>  <div class="message-body">  <div class="content"><pre><code>{&quot;content&quot;: &quot;1|# WorkVault\n2|\n3|`AvaTar-ArTs/iterm2` is the portable seed repository for **WorkVault**, a local-first terminal, AI-session, repository-provenance, and workspace-recovery system.\n4|\n5|The original iTerm2-specific work remains part of the design, but iTerm2 is now treated as a sensor/provider rather than the whole product. WorkVault correlates terminal sessions, agent sessions, processes, repositories, branches, transcripts, tool events, artifacts, research, decisions, incidents, and provenance without making raw private history public by default.\n6|\n7|## Design record\n8|\n9|The architecture is grounded in real working histories rather than synthetic examples.\n10|\n11|- [`docs/CONVERSATION_SYNTHESIS.md`](docs/CONVERSATION_SYNTHESIS.md) — complete design synthesis from the WorkVault/iTerm2 conversation\n12|- [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) — core architecture and runtime model\n13|- [`docs/FIXTURE_CORPUS.md`](docs/FIXTURE_CORPUS.md) — Fiverr, ESO/Poseidon, CoH/LaunchCat, marketplace-agent, and multi-agent iTerm2 golden fixtures\n14|- [`docs/SECURITY_MODEL.md`](docs/SECURITY_MODEL.md) — local-first ingestion, redaction, reference-only evidence, public/private boundaries\n15|- [`schemas/canonical-event.schema.json`](schemas/canonical-event.schema.json) — first executable canonical-event contract\n16|\n17|## First working command: repository hygiene audit\n18|\n19|Install locally:\n20|\n21|```bash\n22|python -m pip install -e .\n23|```\n24|\n25|Scan the current repository:\n26|\n27|```bash\n28|wv github-audit .\n29|```\n30|\n31|Machine-readable output:\n32|\n33|```bash\n34|wv github-audit . --json\n35|```\n36|\n37|Use in CI or automation:\n38|\n39|```bash\n40|wv github-audit . --fail-on private\n41|wv github-audit . --fail-on secret\n42|```\n43|\n44|Current classifications:\n45|\n46|- `SAFE_PUBLIC` — explicitly safe/exportable material\n47|- `REVIEW` — logs, debug output, temp data, backups, or similar material requiring review\n48|- `PRIVATE_REFERENCE` — AI/session/runtime history that should usually remain local/private and be indexed by reference\n49|- `SECRET_ROTATE` — credential files or secret-like content requiring immediate review and likely rotation if committed publicly\n50|\n51|The scanner reports **where** a secret-like signal was found without echoing the matched secret value.\n52|\n53|## Why WorkVault exists\n54|\n55|A terminal window is a control room, not an archive.\n56|\n57|Across the reviewed histories, a single working session can contain:\n58|\n59|```text\n60|research\n61|background agents\n62|code changes\n63|Git commits\n64|failed runs\n65|security incidents\n66|filesystem mutations\n67|model switches\n68|source corrections\n69|GUI actions\n70|queued follow-ups\n71|productization\n72|interrupted work\n73|```\n74|\n75|Flattening that into one transcript loses the actual project state.\n76|\n77|WorkVault preserves the causal structure.\n78|\n79|## Six durable entities\n80|\n81|The conversation initially surfaced many useful concepts. The core was deliberately reduced to six durable entities so the database does not become an ontology maze:\n82|\n83|```text\n84|PROJECT      long-lived canonical effort/product\n85|WORKSTREAM   coherent objective spanning sessions/runs\n86|SESSION      working context from terminal/agent/chat/IDE\n87|RUN          one foreground/background/queued/detached execution\n88|ARTIFACT     produced or materially modified output\n89|RESOURCE     observed/referenced dependency WorkVault may not own\n90|```\n91|\n92|Incidents, decisions, corrections, source status, model changes, drift, milestones, path mutations, and follow-ups are represented primarily as typed events.\n93|\n94|## Canonical event model\n95|\n96|Representative events:\n97|\n98|```text\n99|objective.created\n100|objective.refined\n101|&quot;, &quot;total_lines&quot;: 345, &quot;file_size&quot;: 9643, &quot;truncated&quot;: true, &quot;hint&quot;: &quot;Use offset=101 to continue reading (showing 1-100 of 345 lines)&quot;, &quot;is_binary&quot;: false, &quot;is_image&quot;: false}</code></pre></div>  </div></div>
